    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Summary",
      "html": "<p>This optional unit adds 50 words that occur 12–14 times in the New Testament and are not in Machen&#x27;s lessons: 22 nouns, 18 verbs and 10 other words. Nothing in the course waits for them; they are here so that you can read the New Testament with the lexicon open less often. Learn them on the Words track: recognize, recall, type, type with accents.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Built from words you know",
      "html": "<p>These verbs are a preposition plus a verb from the lessons; the meaning usually follows from the parts: προσδέχομαι (δέχομαι); διαφέρω (φέρω); ἐπιζητέω (ζητέω); καταλαμβάνω (λαμβάνω).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Common confusion",
      "html": "<p>Look-alikes that differ by one letter: καίω (I ignite) and κλαίω (I weep); καπνός (smoke) and καινός (fresh); Μάρθα (Martha) and Μαρία (Mary); Τίτος (Titus) and σῖτος (wheat); τρόπος (way) and τόπος (a place).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Source",
      "html": "<p>Words chosen by their New Testament frequency (MorphGNT); glosses after Jeffrey Dodson&#x27;s Greek-English lexicon (public domain).</p>"
    },
